<h2 class="ds-section-title">Get started</h2>

<div class="ds-grid-2">
  <div class="ds-grid-content">
    <p class="ds-intro-text">
      DB Diff is built for the case a dump and compare cannot handle: a table with millions of rows where you need to
      know which rows drifted, without transferring the table.
    </p>

    <div class="ds-features-grid">
      <div class="ds-feature-card">
        <h3>Three engines</h3>
        <p>PostgreSQL, MySQL and ClickHouse, with one checksum contract across all three</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ds-feature-card">
        <h3>Checksums only</h3>
        <p>Server-side MD5 chunking, so only digests cross the wire when the tables match</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ds-feature-card">
        <h3>Pinpoint drift</h3>
        <p>A differing segment is read row by row and reported as primary keys</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ds-feature-card">
        <h3>Column control</h3>
        <p>Include or exclude columns to leave the noisy ones out of the comparison</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ds-feature-card">
        <h3>CI ready</h3>
        <p>Exit 0 when the tables match, 1 when they differ, 2 when the run failed</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ds-feature-card">
        <h3>Tunable segments</h3>
        <p>Trade query count against how much is read when something differs</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="ds-grid-terminal">
    <div class="ds-install-card">
      <h3>Install in one line</h3>
      <div class="ds-terminal__command">
        <span class="ds-terminal__prompt">$</span> go install matto.club/vetrina/db-diff@latest
      </div>
      <div class="ds-terminal__command">
        <span class="ds-terminal__prompt">$</span> brew tap clubmatto/vetrina https://github.com/clubmatto/vetrina &&
        brew install clubmatto/vetrina/db-diff
      </div>
      <p class="ds-install-note">Requires Go 1.24+ or Homebrew.</p>
    </div>
    <a href="https://github.com/clubmatto/vetrina/blob/main/db-diff/README.md" class="ds-btn-outline">Read the docs</a>
  </div>
</div>

<h2 class="ds-section-title">How it works</h2>

<div class="ds-callout">
  <p class="ds-intro-text">
    DB Diff cuts the table into segments of primary keys and checksums each one on both sides. Equal checksums are
    skipped. A differing segment is read row by row, so the cost follows the number of differing segments rather than
    the size of the table.
  </p>
  <p class="ds-intro-text">
    The comparison runs within one engine. Engines render values their own way, so a cross engine run is refused rather
    than reported as every row changed.
  </p>

  <div class="ds-ctas">
    <a
      href="https://github.com/clubmatto/vetrina/blob/main/db-diff/docs/how-it-works.md"
      class="ds-btn ds-btn--primary"
      >Read the algorithm notes</a
    >
  </div>
</div>

